# Customer Satisfaction Dashboard — Olist Capstone

PORA Academy Cohort 7 · Data Analysis · Group 1 Capstone

A Streamlit app where **every chart is filtered** by the sidebar
**Reporting Year** and **State** selectors.

## What responds to the filters

| Element | Filtered? |
|---|---|
| Headline ("Late deliveries cost you X stars") and the 3 supporting facts | Yes |
| KPI row (orders, delivered, avg review, late, avg delivery days) | Yes |
| Review score distribution | Yes |
| Monthly average review score | Yes |
| Average review score by state (top 10) | Yes |
| On-time vs late by state (top 5) | Yes |
| Punctuality vs satisfaction | Yes |
| Satisfaction by delivery-time bucket (reference line = selection average) | Yes |
| Brazil map (selected states coloured, others greyed; year filtered) | Yes |
| "Insight" line under every chart | Yes — recomputed from the selection |
| Detail & Method diagnostic tables | No — whole-dataset data-quality checks |
| Recommendations tab | No — decisions are based on the whole dataset |

Every filtered query shares one definition (`FILTER_SQL` in `olist_app.py`),
so all charts filter identically. Set both filters to **All** to reproduce
the reference numbers.

## Setup

```bash
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate        # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

## Data

Download the Brazilian E-Commerce Public Dataset by Olist (Kaggle) and put
these four files in a `data/` folder next to `olist_app.py`:

```
data/
├── olist_orders_dataset.csv
├── olist_customers_dataset.csv
├── olist_order_items_dataset.csv
└── olist_order_reviews_dataset.csv
```

To use a different folder: `export OLIST_DATA_DIR=/path/to/csvs`.

## Run

```bash
streamlit run olist_app.py
```

## Environment variables

| Variable | Purpose | Default |
|---|---|---|
| `OLIST_DATA_DIR` | Folder containing the 4 CSVs | `./data` |
| `OLIST_DB_PATH` | SQLite file the app builds | `./olist.db` |
| `OLIST_LOG_LEVEL` | Logging level | `INFO` |

## Reference numbers (filters = All)

Total Orders 99,441 · Delivered 96,478 · Avg Review 4.09 · Late 7,826 ·
Avg Delivery Days 12.56 · On-time 4.294 vs Late 2.566 (gap 1.73 stars).

## Tips for the presentation

- Filtered selections can be small. Read the `n=` labels before drawing
  conclusions (see *Detail & Method → L7*).
- Present the on-time vs late gap as an **association, not proof of
  causation** (*Detail & Method → L1*).
- The Brazil map downloads a public GeoJSON at runtime; it needs internet
  access and degrades to a warning if unavailable.